---
description: Enforce absolute import aliases for hand-written Portal app code
alwaysApply: true
---

# Import Alias

- For hand-written app code, local imports must use absolute aliases: `@/`, `~/`, `#...`, or existing package aliases such as `#scripts/*`.
- Apply this to `pages/`, `layouts/`, `composables/`, `services/`, `stores/`, `models/`, `validations/`, and custom `components/molecules` / `components/organisms`.
- Do not apply this rule to library/generated code such as `components/ui/`, `.nuxt/`, `stories/auto/`, or files created by `shadcn-vue add`.
- Do not add new relative local imports like `../foo` or `./foo` in hand-written app code.

```ts
// Good
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils'
import FormCard from '@/components/organisms/FormCard.vue'

// Bad
import { cn } from '../lib/utils'
import FormCard from './FormCard.vue'
```
